its node1 then node2 (lan-a -> transit -> lan-b)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3 and node4 were given static routes forcing 10.10.1.0/24<->10.10.2.0/24 traffic via node1 (eth1 transit/eth2 lan-a) and node2 (opt1 transit/opt2 lan-b). node1's route table shows 10.10.2.0/24 via the transit link to node2, and node2's route table shows 10.10.1.0/24 via the transit link to node1, confirming the required chain.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-71d74cde25614770\",\"cmd-e17b6ddcd0cc4263\",\"cmd-cdf3615206744e07\",\"cmd-57f03d5bbad441d1\",\"cmd-54a6feaaa9e0405c\",\"cmd-cffc11b219304d49\"]},{\"id\":\"node1-accept-log\",\"requirement\":\"node1 (VyOS) permits the node3->node4 tcp/23 traffic and records the permit\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A VyOS forward-filter rule (accept, log, tcp/23, 10.10.1.0/24 -> 10.10.2.0/24) was committed and rendered into nftables with a log prefix '[ipv4-FWD-filter-10-A]'. A real connection attempt from node3 produced a matching kernel log entry with that prefix (accept, '-A' suffix) for SRC=10.10.1.2 DST=10.10.2.2 DPT=23 SYN, directly showing the permit was recorded.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-14be665a1e474352\",\"cmd-54a6feaaa9e0405c\",\"cmd-68452760813d48ba\",\"cmd-5afcdbf4172a4c0c\"]},{\"id\":\"node2-refuse-log\",\"requirement\":\"node2 (OPNsense) refuses the node3->node4 tcp/23 traffic and records the refusal\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An OPNsense pf rule (block return / reject, log, tcp/23 destined to 10.10.2.0/24, interface opt1) is active per pfctl -sr. The node3 connect attempt returned 'Connection refused' (TCP RST), and node2's filterlog recorded a matching 'block' entry for the same SYN packet (5-tuple, IP ID 57047), directly evidencing both the refusal and its log record.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-cdd6ba1afeaf4c48\",\"cmd-cffc11b219304d49\",\"cmd-6653bfec46e04b46\",\"cmd-4dc898e4fbee4413\"]},{\"id\":\"correlated-log-pair\",\"requirement\":\"Show the pair of log entries produced by one attempt so the stop point is evident from the records alone\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For a single node3 connect attempt, node1's kernel log ('[ipv4-FWD-filter-10-A] ... SRC=10.10.1.2 DST=10.10.2.2 ... DPT=23 ... ID=57047 SYN') and node2's filterlog ('block ... 10.10.1.2,10.10.2.2,35080,23 ... ID 57047') were pulled and correlated on identical IP ID and 5-tuple, directly demonstrating the packet was accepted at node1 and blocked at node2 using the records alone.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-68452760813d48ba\",\"cmd-5afcdbf4172a4c0c\",\"cmd-4dc898e4fbee4413\",\"cmd-47f5f30ad0e44a27\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol for node1 (VyOS)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id (e636d872...) and healthy config captured, reboot acknowledged, connection timed out confirming the disruption, post-restart boot_id changed (714321cc...), and interfaces/routes/ip_forward/nftables accept+log rule were re-verified intact after restart, plus a second correlated accept/block log pair was captured post-restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c823d076de9140a0\",\"cmd-f193eafd4d774234\",\"cmd-61b2d1fe47a147ec\",\"cmd-70ad950117b7461c\",\"cmd-5200b2d94b2f49ed\",\"cmd-96e3c2d8525e4858\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol for node2 (OPNsense)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart kern.boottime baseline captured, shutdown -r acknowledged, post-restart kern.boottime changed, and interface addresses, static route, and block/log pf rule re-verified intact; a post-restart filterlog block entry for the second attempt was also captured.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-51ebc1e146e94b30\",\"cmd-ecd0a40ee98b423a\",\"cmd-1e8a16a70a864a92\",\"cmd-e0a3b99920974d85\",\"cmd-e0b2ce4c86de4f6e\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol for node3 (RHEL7)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id captured, reboot acknowledged, post-restart boot_id changed, and eth1 static IP/route and connectivity to node1 confirmed recovered; node3 was subsequently used to re-run the connect attempt successfully.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c6bda03fa20e4d08\",\"cmd-e255a4be527342fd\",\"cmd-7fe02565f48f499b\",\"cmd-9d16c84f70d7483e\",\"cmd-ea57a926076542d6\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol for node4 (RHEL7)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id captured, reboot acknowledged, post-restart boot_id changed, and eth1 static IP/route confirmed recovered after restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fb973d23dc9548d1\",\"cmd-70fc26e02be741f8\",\"cmd-11d5b101109a49b2\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Executor commands were mostly read-only discovery (OPNsense filter/rule source inspection) or config commands that directly furthered the task. A handful of VyOS 'set' commands failed with 'Set failed' due to syntax exploration (cmd-abbc34dd4eda48e7, cmd-bce2311f5e1e403e) but these did not mutate persisted config and were promptly corrected (cmd-17b22e7644fc4b56) before commit. Several failed nmcli con add attempts on node3/node4 (invalid ipv6 method, then insufficient privilege) created no connections and were corrected with sudo (cmd-cdf3615206744e07/cmd-57f03d5bbad441d1). On node2, a PHP script /root/setup_node2.php was iteratively authored and repaired (base64 decode, sed/python edits) before finally executing successfully (cmd-cdd6ba1afeaf4c48); this script file appears to have been left on node2's filesystem as residue, though it is a low-risk artifact directly tied to the required configuration change and not flagged by the /tmp-scoped temp-file inventory. No destructive actions, security weakening, or broad/unbounded mutations were observed; restarts were performed one node at a time with confirmed recovery.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-abbc34dd4eda48e7\",\"cmd-bce2311f5e1e403e\",\"cmd-17b22e7644fc4b